    "result_text": "The full test suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification side-effect on successful owner creation in `ClinicServiceImpl.java`:\n\n1. **Added a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java:60-61`), mirroring the existing `AUDIT` channel convention.\n\n2. **Emitted the welcome notification** inside the existing `if (isNew)` block of the create path, right after the audit lines:\n   ```java\n   NOTIFY.info(\"welcome owner id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n   ```\n\nThis emits a line on the `NOTIFY` logger containing both the owner id and the memberId, only on a successful create (the `isNew` branch, reached after all validation/quota checks and the `save`). The acceptance test `coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes and `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures.",
